; BLOCK (alias of -BLOCK) defines Pezzo from a line; -BLOCK redefines it with
; Yes from a circle, then No and Enter (default N) end the command without
; changes, and U brings back the first definition (PT20, #703).
; Prompts and the "redefined" message from autocad-blocchi.txt (dxf-test-file
; 1ad04b0, block RIDEFINITO), in English as Block "<name>" redefined of PT21.
; Every entity is drawn before the first block, and the base point is 0,0.
LINE
0,0
10,0

CIRCLE
30,0
5
BLOCK
Pezzo
0,0
5,0

!report
-BLOCK
Pezzo
Yes
0,0
35,0

!report
-BLOCK
Pezzo
No
-BLOCK
Pezzo

!report
U
